{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L77-L114","doc":"**Brane-tower convergence via q-Laplacian decay** ([`prop:brane-tower-q-laplacian-decay`]).\n\nFor `q > 1` the remainder of the brane tower past the local\nsingle-jet term is bounded by the manuscript's closed form\n`ℏ_q⁴‖ρ‖·q⁻²/(1 − q⁻²)`.\n\n**Derived**: the geometric majorant `∑' k, M·r^{k+1}` supplied by the\ntermwise-decay input is *summed* here to its closed form\n`M·r/(1 − r)` via `tsum_geometric_of_lt_one` — the actual `=` step of\nthe manuscript's geometric-series tail. Not a restatement of a class\nfield. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:brane-tower-q-laplacian-decay","label":"prop:brane-tower-q-laplacian-decay","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/brane-tower-q-laplacian-decay.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.remainder_le_geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.remainder_le_geom","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Termwise exponential-decay input.** The tail past the single-jet\nterm is majorised, level by level, by the geometric series with\ncoefficient `M = ℏ_q⁴‖ρ‖` — the `.md`'s displayed\n`∑ ℏ_q^{2n}·q^{-2(n-1)}` bound. This is the genuine physical\nhypothesis (bounded iterated-Laplacian modes), NOT the closed\nform. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Contraction: `r < 1` (i.e. `q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Positivity: `0 ≤ r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The ratio is the substrate `q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.r","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The geometric ratio of the tail decay, `r = q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.delta1_rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.delta1_rho","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The single-jet (n = 1) local Laplacian contribution `Δ⁽¹⁾(ρ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.T_rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.T_rho","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The brane-tower sum `T(ρ) = ∑_{n ≥ 1} ℏ_q^{2n} Δ⁽ⁿ⁾(ρ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.q_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.q_real","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Substrate parameter `q` (archimedean, over `ℝ`: the bound is a\nreal-valued norm inequality, §7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.rho_L2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.rho_L2","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L51-L51","doc":"L² norm of the Reeb-bundle density `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.hbar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.hbar_q","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Substrate q-Planck constant `ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.BraneTowerQLaplacianDecayContext","kind":"class","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay.lean#L43-L75","doc":"Dual-feasibility / decay **inputs** for the brane-tower bound. Every\nfield is a genuine hypothesis supplied by the q-Laplacian spectrum;\nthe manuscript's closed-form remainder bound is **derived** in\n`brane_tower_q_laplacian_decay`, not carried here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}